Package: nvda-rdp-common
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}
Description: NVDA's RDAccess on Linux: code shared by the client and the server
 RDAccess carries NVDA's speech and braille over RDP. This package holds the
 Python code shared by nvda-rdp-client and nvda-rdp-server: the framing and
 the RDAccess protocol.

Package: nvda-rdp-freerdp-plugin
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: NVDA's RDAccess on Linux: FreeRDP plugin of the RDAccess channels
 A FreeRDP 3 dynamic virtual channel plugin, nvda-rdp-dvc, that passes the
 NVDA-SPEECH and NVDA-BRAILLE channels to nvda-rdp-client. It works with
 xfreerdp3 and Remmina.

Package: nvda-rdp-client
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${python3:Depends},
 nvda-rdp-common (= ${source:Version}),
 nvda-rdp-freerdp-plugin (>= ${source:Version}),
 at-spi2-core,
 gir1.2-atspi-2.0,
 pipewire-bin,
 python3-brlapi,
 python3-gi,
 python3-pyatspi,
 python3-speechd,
 speech-dispatcher,
Recommends: brltty, freerdp3-x11 | remmina
Suggests: x11-xserver-utils, xdotool
Description: NVDA's RDAccess on Linux: client for a remote NVDA's speech and braille
 nvda-rdp-client speaks a remote Windows NVDA through Speech Dispatcher and
 shows its braille through BRLTTY, from an RDP session with the
 nvda-rdp-dvc plugin. A systemd user unit keeps it running for the whole
 graphical session.

Package: nvda-rdp-server
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${python3:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 nvda-rdp-common (= ${source:Version}),
 gdm3 (>= 49),
 gir1.2-glib-2.0,
 gnome-remote-desktop (>= 49),
 liblouis-data,
 orca (>= 49),
 python3-gi,
 python3-louis,
 python3-speechd,
 speech-dispatcher,
 systemd,
Description: NVDA's RDAccess on Linux: Orca for NVDA users over GNOME Remote Desktop
 For an NVDA user connecting with RDP to GDM's remote login of GNOME Remote
 Desktop: in those sessions, Orca speaks and writes braille through the
 user's NVDA, by RDAccess. Local sessions keep their usual speech and
 braille. It needs GNOME 49 or later.
